vacuum chamber boundaries

and seals each run with encryption + provenance, authored under:

C. MATTHEW BLACKWELL — Independent Designer

1.2 Top-level architecture

Core Simulation KernelEvolves system state over time using numerical integration.

Constraint ManagerEncodes and enforces physical limits (thermal, structural, power, plasma, environment).

Scenario Definition LayerDescribes geometry, materials, power sources, plasma regions, and chamber configuration.

Persistence & Encryption LayerStores runs as tamper‑evident records (hash + signature).

Interface Layer (CLI + optional GUI)Controls simulations, validation, and reporting.

1.3 Core modules

Module: ThermalEngine

Inputs: geometry, material properties, heat sources.

Outputs: temperature fields over time.

Constraints: max allowable temperature per region.

Module: StructuralEngine

Inputs: loads, geometry, material fatigue curves.

Outputs: stress/strain, fatigue accumulation.

Constraints: yield limits, fatigue life thresholds.

Module: PowerEngine

Inputs: power sources, loads, storage.

Outputs: power usage, reserves, efficiency.

Constraints: max draw, minimum reserve, duty cycles.

Module: PlasmaEngine

Inputs: plasma density, temperature, fields, chamber geometry.

Outputs: stability metrics, interaction forces.

Constraints: instability thresholds, wall loading limits.

Module: EnvironmentEngine

Inputs: chamber pressure, boundaries, external conditions.

Outputs: environment state.

Constraints: vacuum integrity, allowable leakage.

Module: ConstraintManager

Aggregates all module outputs.

Evaluates constraint inequalities each timestep.

Flags violations and can trigger mitigation (e.g., power throttling).

1.4 Encryption & provenance

RunMetadata:

scenario config

model versions

timestamps

authorship:C. MATTHEW BLACKWELL — Independent Designer

Process:

Serialize metadata + key state snapshots.

Compute SHA‑256 hash.

Sign hash with private key → signature block.

Store {metadata, hash, signature} with simulation outputs.

Verification:

Recompute hash from stored metadata + states.

Verify signature with public key.

If mismatch → run is tampered.

1.5 Interface layer

CLI commands:

simulate

Args: --config, --duration, --dt.

Runs scenario, enforces constraints, writes sealed record.

validate-run

Args: --input.

Verifies hash + signature, checks constraint compliance.

export-report

Args: --input, --format.

Outputs human‑readable summary (limits, margins, violations).

Optional GUI:

Plots: temperature vs. time, stress maps, power curves, plasma stability, constraint margins.

